Usage: validate_assets [--assets DIRECTORY] [--json]
       validate_assets [--assets DIRECTORY] --type TYPE --file KEY [--scene-budget N] [--json]
       validate_assets --help
Default: validate Feature Lab's shipped assets, references and both levels.
Single file: TYPE is scene, tilemap, animation, texture, font or sound.
KEY is relative to the asset root. Only the chosen format is checked;
references and gameplay are not checked. Extensions do not select the format.
Scene budget: 0..4096, default 4096; only valid with --type scene.
--json writes one engine_asset_validation_v1 report to stdout. Argument errors
remain text on stderr (exit 2); content/root failures produce JSON (exit 1).
Uses assets beside the executable or ../share/feature_lab by default.
Read-only; no display/audio device or fallback assets. Bundle shader checks
read sources only; OpenGL compilation and playability need runtime tests.
Exit codes: 0 valid, 1 content/root failure, 2 invalid arguments.
